=2 Walkthrough
!Yhoator Jungle-map.jpg|right|Yhoator Jungle Map
!Ifrit's Cauldron-map1.jpg|right|Ifrit's Cauldron Map
Trade enough {p:Crystals} to the {p:Conquest NPC} to raise your Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the {n:Gate Guard}.
* Speak to {p:Naji} for a cutscene.
** You may need to speak to him several times to get the correct cutscene.
* Head to {z:Norg} and speak with {p:Gilgamesh} behind the **Oaken Door** at (K-8). Continue speaking with him until he mentions {@i:Frag Rock|1160} {i:Frag Rocks|Frag Rock|1160}.
** **{c=red:Note:}** You will receive up to 6 {@i:Frag Rock|1160} {i:Frag Rocks|Frag Rock|1160} per fight.
* Obtain 1 {@i:Adaman Ore|646} {i:Adaman Ore|Adaman Ore|646} for every 6 players in your party/alliance.
** These may be obtained from the {z:Auction House} ({@g:Auction House} > Materials > Smithing)
** If none available on {z:Auction House}, they can be mined in {z:Ifrit's Cauldron}. Be prepared for a long mining session as the drop is 'Very Rare'
* Proceed to {z:Yhoator Jungle} (I-5) and enter {z:Ifrit's Cauldron}.
** Quick Travel options:
** {z:Ifrit's Cauldron} {p:Home Point} #1, then cast {s:Escape} and zone back in.
** {p:Unity Warp} (Level 122) > {z:Yhoator Jungle} > hug the right wall. It's a short ride.
** Alternatively, you may use the {p:Elshimo Uplands} {p:Outpost Warp} or {p:Survival Guide}.
* You will have to reach a **???** which isn't too far inside (Map 1, H-7). You may need use {s:Sneak} and {s:Invisible} (still useful inside the Cauldron at level 99 to avoid aggroing) to get there, as there are {p:Bats|Bat} and {p:Bombs|Bomb} in the way.
* Once inside, head left at the first intersection, and then on the next intersection go right. The **???** is in a lava flow area around (H-7), Map 1.
* Buff up and prepare to fight. Trading an {@i:Adaman Ore|646} {i:Adaman Ore|Adaman Ore|646} to the **???** will spawn a lvl 65 {p:Bomb}, {m:Magma}, and {m:Salamander}, a {m:Lizard} NM.
** {s:Barfira} is recommended.
** The Lizard is much weaker than the Bomb.
** {s:Sneak} pulling is recommended, as you only need to defeat the Bomb, and you do not need to wait for the Lizard to depop.
** Magma may use {s:Self-Destruct}.
* Upon defeating {m:Magma}, it will drop 6 Rare/Ex {@i:Frag Rock|1160} {i:Frag Rocks|Frag Rock|1160}.
** If doing this fight for more than 6 people, you will need to spawn them again.
* When everyone has their {i:Frag Rock|Frag Rock|1160}, head back to {z:Norg} and trade it to {p:Gilgamesh} for a cutscene.
* Head back to {p:Naji} for a final cutscene and your reward.

